// endpoint_load_page_in_editor.proto — LoadPageInEditor: the user asked for a
// held-back page. WEB section. The webhost's load button calls this, so the
// page is loaded by the EDITOR, which owns which pages the host holds.
//
// WHY A PAGE IS HELD BACK. A cold-gated workspace's page is not loaded when
// the user switches to it (owner request, 2026-10-30): the gate is drawn by
// the webhost on its own (host/gate.ts), and loading the feed behind it costs
// the web process a whole page for a workspace the user is often only passing
// on the way to another. The webhost draws a load button where the page would
// be, and the click asks for the page through here.
//
// WHY THE EDITOR LOADS IT. Emacs owns the desired state of the host (which
// pages it holds, and at which URL), and replays it whenever the host loads
// (lisp/webhost.el). A page the webhost loaded on its own would be one Emacs
// does not know it holds: never unloaded, never announced unloading, and lost
// on the next replay. So the click is relayed on the workspace's host stream
// as `load_page_requested`, and Emacs loads the page through the same path a
// switch takes.

